ld S. Hancock, the Democratic candidate. Garfield receives 214 Electoral College votes to 155 for Hancock, but barely wins the popular vote with a majority of only 7,023 voters.\n\nBuy Chronology\n\n1881\n\nJanuary 25, 1881 - Thomas Edison and Alexander Graham Bell form the Oriental Telephone Company.\n\nMay"
